=== REASONING ===
Slice 0051 layers an opt-in Helix narrator over the existing SoftwareUpdatesPage without replacing or branching the
deterministic baseline. ADR-015 invariants honoured by construction:

I3 baseline intact: AISoftwareUpdateChangelogSummarizer is rendered ABOVE the existing timeline as an additional
   FadeIn block. The existing MetricCard + GlassPanel timeline + external release-note links are unchanged. No
   conditional `{aiOn ? <AI/> : <Baseline/>}` branching exists; the baseline is always present.

I4 zero egress (off mode): The withAiFeature HOC returns null when useAiEnabled('software-update-changelog-summarizer')
   returns false. useAiStream is therefore never instantiated, so no /ai/* fetch is enqueued. The off-mode test
   verifies the wrapper renders an empty container.

I5 hidden UI: data-testid="ai-feature-software-update-changelog-summarizer-root" is the wrapper from withAiFeature;
   it is absent from the DOM in off mode (proven by TestSoftwareUpdateSummaryAIOffShowsRawChangelogOnly).

I6 404 routes: POST /api/v1/ai/software-updates/summarize is wrapped by ai.GuardedHandler (see
   mountAIRoutes @ internal/api/ai_routes.go:584 area). The guard returns 404 BEFORE the handler runs when
   ai_mode='off' or the per-feature toggle is off. The Go off-mode test asserts this directly.

I7 per-feature: Registry entry has DefaultOn=false. The toggle is independent of the global ai_mode flag — both
   gates must be open. Tests cover both halves of the gate (mode='off' with toggle on, mode='cloud' with toggle off).

I10 type system: TypeScript interface for the request body matches the Go DTO (vehicle_id: number → vehicle_id int64).
    aigen --check confirms web/src/ai/features.ts mirrors the Go registry.

I12 client/bg: ai_update_notes_indexer is a fail-closed cron stub (RunAIUpdateNotesIndexer) that re-checks ai_mode
    + per-feature toggle on every tick. Settings-read failures fail closed (Skipped=1). No background fan-out
    is performed yet (the per-version embed loop lands in a future indexer slice); the gate + telemetry envelope
    ship today so the off-mode invariant is structurally provable.

P1-P10 alignment:
  - P1 (provider port): Strategy never imports a provider adapter directly; the dispatcher resolves via aiToolRegistry.
  - P4 (dispatcher loop): Handler invokes dispatch.Run with the strategy + tool registry; no bespoke loop.
  - P5 (decorator chain): Provider calls flow through redact → rate-limit → cost-cap → audit → trace via the
    decorator chain installed in NewAIToolRegistry/NewAIDispatcher (no per-handler wrapping).
  - P6 (backend guard / frontend HOC): ai.GuardedHandler on backend, withAiFeature on frontend.
  - P8 (eval goldens): 3 deterministic goldens at internal/ai/strategies/software-update-changelog-summarizer/goldens.yaml
    + 3 canned mock responses under canned/. ai-eval --feature software-update-changelog-summarizer = 3/3 PASS.
  - P9 (registry): Entry added with all surface metadata; CoverageOK passes.
  - P10 (baseline coexistence): Baseline rendered unconditionally; AI section is opt-in addendum.
  - P11 (wired-or-absent): The component imports useAiStream and is wired end-to-end against
    /api/v1/ai/software-updates/summarize. No placeholder strings (W1 self-check = 0).
  - P12 (no-placeholder-buttons): Button's disabled prop is `!canStart || stream.state === 'streaming'`,
    a computed expression. The on-mode wiring test asserts both the enabled and computed-disabled paths.

Per-request scope binding (defence-in-depth, mirrors predictive-maintenance R-class):
  The handler installs WithScopedSoftwareUpdateChangelogWindow{VehicleID, Limit} into ctx BEFORE dispatch.Run
  starts. The query_vehicle_software tool's Execute REJECTS any LLM-supplied vehicle_id mismatch ⇒ a
  prompt-injected "summarize vehicle 99 instead" cannot exfiltrate cross-vehicle data. The retrieve_update_notes
  tool's Validate ALSO clamps the LLM-requested limit to the scope window's Limit. The system prompt explicitly
  refuses cross-vehicle requests ("Refuse politely if asked to summarize, modify, or compare any vehicle other
  than the one named in the request").

F7 source-type allowlist:
  retrieve_update_notes restricts source_types to {software_update, docs}. The unexported constants
  softwareUpdateSourceUpdate + softwareUpdateSourceDocs are aggregated into a slice (lex order) and validated
  at the tool boundary. Forward-compat: NOT promoted to rag.Source* constants — keeps the F7 contract tight.

F8 redaction:
  PolicyChatbot() (Allow=nil, Mode=ModeRedactedTags) is the round-trip redaction policy. Release notes are
  PUBLIC text (no PII); the policy strips VINs, coordinates, place names, IPs, emails, phones, MACs to defend
  against accidental leak via user-context strings (e.g., a vehicle's display_name a user set to "John Doe's Tesla").

HX (Helix UX) compliance:
  - Component renders through AIFeatureCard, NOT a bespoke GlassPanel + Button + AiOutputPanel composition.
  - buttonLabel="Summarize updates" (the per-feature verb). The card composes the accessible name as
    "Ask Helix · Summarize updates"; tests use UNANCHORED regex `/Summarize updates/i`.
  - badgeLabel="Helix" (not "AI") in the user-visible header.
  - All user-visible i18n keys say "Helix" not "AI" (softwareUpdates.aiNarration.{title,description,button,badge,noVehicleHint}).

